.TH MOUNT_NFS3 8 "FreeMiNT" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
mount_nfs3 \- mount an NFS version 3 file system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount_nfs3
[
.B \-rvnf
] [
.B \-o
.I options
]
.I host:/remotedir localdir
.br
.B mount_nfs3 \-u
[
.B \-vn
]
.I localdir
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mount_nfs3
attaches the directory
.I remotedir
exported by
.I host
to the local directory
.IR localdir ,
using version 3 of the NFS protocol (RFC 1813).
.PP
It asks the server's
.BR rpc.mountd (8)
over version 3 of the MOUNT protocol for a file handle and passes that
handle, together with the mount options, to the
.B nfs3.xfs
kernel driver.
.I localdir
must be below
.BR u:\enfs3 ,
the directory the driver installs itself into; it is created by the
driver and need not exist beforehand.
.PP
For NFS version 2 servers use
.BR mount_nfs (8)
instead. The two protocols and the two drivers are independent and may
be used at the same time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r
Mount the file system read only. Same as
.BR "\-o ro" .
.TP
.BI \-o " options"
A comma separated list of options, see
.B "MOUNT OPTIONS"
below.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose. Also prints the size of the file handle the server returned and
the authentication flavours it accepts.
.TP
.B \-n
Do not update
.BR \eetc\emtab .
.TP
.B \-f
Fake the mount: only update
.BR \eetc\emtab .
.TP
.B \-u
Unmount
.I localdir
instead of mounting.
.SH MOUNT OPTIONS
.TP
.BR ro ", " rw
Mount read only or read write. The default is
.BR rw .
.TP
.BR suid ", " nosuid
Honour or ignore the set-uid bit on files of this mount.
.TP
.BI rsize= n
.TP
.BI wsize= n
Preferred read and write transfer size in bytes. The driver asks the
server for its limits with FSINFO3 at mount time and reduces these
values if the server cannot handle them. The default is 4096.
.TP
.BI timeo= n
Initial RPC timeout in tenths of a second. The default is 2 seconds.
.TP
.BI retrans= n
Number of retransmissions before the request fails. The default is 5.
.TP
.BI port= n
Port the NFS service listens on. The default is 2049.
.TP
.BI actimeo= n
How long attributes may be cached, in tenths of a second. The default is
30 seconds.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mount_nfs3 fileserver:/srv/atari u:\enfs3\eatari
mount_nfs3 \-o ro,rsize=8192 fileserver:/pub u:\enfs3\epub
mount_nfs3 \-u u:\enfs3\eatari
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B \eetc\emtab
table of mounted file systems
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mount_nfs (8),
.BR mtab (5),
.BR exports (5),
RFC 1813
.SH BUGS
Only AUTH_UNIX authentication and UDP transport are supported.
.PP
Files beyond 2 GB cannot be read or written, because MiNT's file
position is a signed 32 bit value.
